# Nothing here is required. The game runs with no configuration at all —
# locally and on Vercel — by keeping rooms in the server's memory.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: durable room storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In memory, a room lives only as long as the serverless instance holding it.
# That is handled gracefully (clients re-register their seat and the round
# restarts — see the README), but if you would rather rooms simply never be
# lost, point these at any Upstash-compatible Redis and the app will use it
# instead. No code change; /api/health will report "storage": "redis".
#
# Note that Vercel's Storage tab bills these through Vercel. Upstash's own
# dashboard is a separate signup, and names the same two values
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL and UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN — either pair works.

# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
